cial case;\n    - `dao.stream.ringbuffer` added, as r7 puts `ringbuffer:168` there;\n    - `dao.stream.udp` and `dao.stream.ws.browser` dropped;\n  - **entropy row:** `dao.await` and `yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve` dropped;\n  - **timers row:** `dao.jing.content.async` dropped;\n  - **runtime-prereq row:** `dao.space.schema` dropped.\n\n  None of the dropped names was in the closure, so dropping them changes\n  no tag.\n- **`docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn`:** regenerated\n  by the tool (32 changed lines each).\n  - The legend gains `:dialect-arm` and `:profile-consumer`.\n  - Each of the 16 files now has its r7 class. The nine moved from\n    `:none` (or, for `yin.vm` and `yang.php`, from\n    `:consumer`/`:deferred-gensym` alone) to include `:profile-consumer`.\n    The dialect files gained `:dialect-arm`.\n  - `ringbuffer` gained `:external-stream-seam`.\n  - Totals, shared count and file lists are byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **F2 count wording.** The gate's `list-2` docstring already reads \"21\n  inside the closure (dao.await and yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve are outside\n  it)\". This matches r7 §3.2: the gate uses the transitive closure, and\n  the five sites outside it are inputs to the deferred design. The data\n  is unchanged and the comment already says this; I made no further\n  wording edit.\n\n## Results (all run in the foreground in the worktree)\n\n```\n$ clojure -M:test -n dao.host.gate-test\nRan 10 tests containing 293 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n$ clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb ...}}' -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure --check   # before regenerating\nSTALE: docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn ...cljs.edn ...cljd.edn    (expected: tags changed)\n$ ... -m host-boundary.closure            # regenerate\nclj   total 142 shared 133 lane-specific 9\ncljs  total 140 shared 133 lane-specific 7\ncljd  total 141 shared 133 lane-specific 8\nshared (all three lanes): 133\n$ ... -m host-boundary.closure --check    -> exit 0\n\n$ bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj --check\n18 files\ncorpus identical to docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn   -> exit 0\n```\n\nclj-kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings. cljstyle check is clean.\n\n**The new check fails when it should.** The probe is\n`target/h0/probe/retag_neg.clj`. It uses `with-redefs` on `list-1` and\nruns `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms`:\n\n- With `yin/vm.cljc` set to `:h0-unlisted`, the run gives\n  `{:pass 227, :fail 2}`. The two failures name the file, the unknown\n  category, and the slice that category cannot allow.\n- With `yin/vm.cljc` set to `:clears \"H9\"`, the run gives\n  `{:pass 228, :fail 1}`.\n\n**JVM lane count.** I did not re-run the full lane; r7 says it need not be\nre-run beyond the gate. No deftest was added, so the tests stay at\n**4131**. Assertions should rise by exactly +228, from 286103 to\n**286331**. That figure is derived, not measured.\n\n## r7 points I could not implement literally, or that disagree with the code\n\n1. **\"No tool change\" vs \"retag the committed closure class tags\".** The\n   closure files never held `:h0-unlisted`; that tag was only in the test.\n   The class tags come from the tool's `class-rows` data. Adding r7's two\n   §3.1 rows and keeping `--check` green therefore required editing that\n   data. I changed only data; the traversal and output format are\n   untouched. Leaving the tool alone would have meant either hand-editing\n   generated files, which `--check` would then flag, or leaving the nine\n   tagged `:none`, which the new list-1 check now refuses.\n2. **`ringbuffer.cljc:168` is placed differently in two sections.** §3.1\n   puts it in the seams row; §8.1 puts it in the \"dialect arms\" row. I\n   followed each section in its own artefact: closure class\n   `:external-stream-seam` (§3.1) and list-1 category `:dialect-arm`\n   (§8.1). Both say \"retained, no slice\", so nothing behaves differently,\n   but the Architect may want one name.\n3. **r7 §3.2 lists the 13 print calls in `main.cljc` as \"`println`,\n   `print`, `flush`, `js/console.log`\".** In the code they are 8\n   `println`, 1 `print` and 4 `js/console.log`. The gate does not count\n   `flush`; `main.cljc` has one `(flush)`. The count of 13 is right; the\n   word `flush` is not.\n4. **`yang/php.cljc` line numbers.** §3.1 and §8.1 cite `:95,98`, which\n   are the conditional sites the gate reports. The behaviour-change text\n   cites `js/parseInt` at `:100`, which is the cljs arm inside the `:98`\n   conditional. These are consistent, just two granularities.\n5. **The six names.** As r7 says, none was ever on the generated list 1,\n   and the equality test keeps it that way. The tool's class rows also no\n   longer name them. The §8.3 codec row still names\n   `dao.stream.ws.browser`, because §8.3 itself does (\"four ws\n   adapters\"); it matches no closure file.\n\nNot done:\n- no design-doc edit;\n- no `src/` behaviour change;\n- no `deps.edn` or `bb.edn` change;\n- no full-lane re-run;\n- no stage, commit or push.\n\nReport: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792523065000-engineer-host-boundary-h0-retag.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\n# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\n\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\n\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\n\n### A. Logic & Correctness\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\n\n### B. Security & Credentials\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\n\n### C. Architecture & API Design\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\n\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\n\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\n\n---\n\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\n\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\n2. **Explain the \"Why\"**: Don't just say \"change this\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\").\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-39QoaQZ8' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-21 02:24:43.161 xcodebuild[12922:78483895]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-21 02:24:43.340 xcodebuild[12922:78483894] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-l9SfdKuJ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-21 02:24:43.868 xcodebuild[12926:78483907]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-21 02:24:44.049 xcodebuild[12926:78483906] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn  |  32 ++---\n docs/design/host-boundary/closure-cljd.edn |  32 ++---\n docs/design/host-boundary/closure-cljs.edn |  32 ++---\n src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj          |  37 +++---\n test/dao/host/gate_test.clj                | 196 +++++++++++++++++------------\n 5 files changed, 181 insertions(+), 148 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
