oes not, and   |\n   460\t|                                                     |                                        | becomes exact on all three. The index comparator keeps   |\n   520\t\n   521\t### 3.3 Exempt dialect syntax\n   522\t\n   523\tNot host contact; the H0 gate exempts them by pattern: `catch` type arms;\n   524\t`^long`/`^bytes`/`^String` hints; protocol and interface names in `deftype`\n   525\tbodies and `print-method`; `exists?`; `js-obj`/`(Object.)` opaque sentinels;\n   526\trequire arms whose only purpose is an alias.\n   527\t\n   528\t## 4. The host-implementation contract\n   529\t\n   530\t### 4.1 Stream implementations and their seams (external contact)\n   531\t\n   532\tUnchanged from the tree for sockets (V) and listed for completeness; the\n   533\tstorage, entropy and parser rows are deferred (§9).\n   534\t\n   535\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   536\t| Implementation             | Portable core (V)                          | Seam value a host supplies                            | Status                      |\n   537\t+============================+============================================+=======================================================+=============================+\n   538\t| Ring buffer, memory log,   | `dao.stream.ringbuffer`, `.memory_log`,    | None. (They mint identities today, §3.2: deferred.)   | Existing                    |\n   539\t| remote channel, waitset,   | `.remote_channel`, `.waitset`, `.observe`, |                                                       |                             |\n   540\t| middleware, apply          | `.middleware`, `.apply`                    |                                                       |                             |\n   541\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   542\t| WebSocket                  | `dao.stream.ws`                            | `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (`host.cljc:20-33`)     | Existing                    |\n   543\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   544\t| Datagram and UDP           | `dao.stream.datagram`, `.udp`              | `bind!` (`datagram.cljc:15-23`)                       | Existing                    |\n   545\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   546\t| Durable journal and the    | `dao.stream.journal` over `dao.jing.file`  | Deferred (§9.2)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   547\t| storage beneath it         | and `store.fs`                             |                                                       |                             |\n   548\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   549\t| Entropy                    | Deferred                                   | Deferred (§9.1)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   550\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   551\t| Parser stage               | `yang.python.antlr.*`                      | Deferred (§9.3)                                       | Deferred                    |\n   552\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   553\t| wasm import surface        | `dao.stream.wasm.md` §1                    | The seven imports                                     | Existing spec               |\n   554\t+----------------------------+--------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   555\t\n   556\tSeam rule (`abi.md` §6-§7 as acceptance): a seam entry is implementation-\n   557\tprivate, called only by the stream implementation that owns it; it takes\n   558\thost arguments and returns or deposits plain data; it never invokes\n   559\tapplication code; it classifies host errors into data; what it cannot do it\n   560\tanswers as a qualified unsupported outcome. A map of functions that portable\n   561\tapplication code calls to reach the world is a host service and is rejected\n   562\t(`abi.md:143-148`); none exists in H0-H4.\n   563\t\n   564\t### 4.2 The primitive profile: exact manifest (P)\n   565\t\n   566\t`dao.host.*` (OQ2 adopted) is a namespace family whose files contain only\n   567\treader-conditional entries and docstrings stating each entry's law, kind (P\n   568\tpure, M mutating per §2.4) and oracle. Table A is the profile (76 entries);\n   569\ttable B the portable code replacing host libraries; table C the runtime\n   570\tprerequisites.\n   571\t\n   572\t**Table A: profile entries.**\n   573\t\n   574\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   575\t| Namespace          | Entries (consolidated from, V)                                                                       | N   | Slice |\n   576\t+====================+======================================================================================================+=====+=======+\n   577\t| `dao.host.integer` | From `yin.vm.integer.host` (all 25, P): `big-carrier?`, `exact-integer?`, `safe-native?`,            | 28  | H1    |\n   578\t|                    | `host-float?`, `nan-float?`, `infinite-float?`, `promote`, `from-native`, `demote`, `to-native`,     |     |       |\n   579\t|                    | `native->double`, `trunc-native`, `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `quot-trunc`, `rem-trunc`, `compare-big`,     |     |       |\n   580\t|                    | `bit-and-big`, `bit-or-big`, `bit-xor-big`, `shift-left-big`, `shift-right-big`,                     |     |       |\n   581\t|                    | `magnitude-bit-length`, `to-radix-string`; from `cbor.cljc:112-254` (P): `parse-decimal` (digit      |     |       |\n   582\t|                    | string to big, refuses otherwise), `gcd`, `magnitude-bytes` (fresh bytes). `debruijn_code.cljc:315`  |     |       |\n   583\t|                    | reads `big-carrier?` (H2).                                                                           |     |       |\n   584\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   585\t| `dao.host.float`   | P: `float64->bits` (16 hex, big-endian), `bits->float64`, `finite?`, `integral?`, `fields` (sign,    | 5   | H1    |\n   586\t|                    | biased exponent, fraction big) from `cbor.cljc:525-560`, `debruijn.cljc:855-885`,                    |     |       |\n   587\t|                    | `debruijn_code.cljc:232-242` (little-endian hex becomes a portable byte reversal over                |     |       |\n   588\t|                    | `float64->bits`, H2), `data.cljc:77-92`.                                                             |     |       |\n   589\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   590\t| `dao.host.number`  | The Jing numeric carriers and their host construction and access, from `cbor.cljc:342-460,483-632`   | 10  | H1    |\n   591\t|                    | (P): `float64-of`, `float-value`, `decimal?`, `decimal-of` (exponent, mantissa; refuses outside the  |     |       |\n   592\t|                    | JVM scale window, `:552-574`), `decimal-exponent`, `decimal-mantissa`, `ratio?`, `ratio-of`          |     |       |\n   593\t|                    | (reduced, sign on numerator, zero denominator refused), `ratio-numerator`, `ratio-denominator`; the  |     |       |\n   594\t|                    | `Float64`, `Rational`, `Decimal` deftypes move with them (table C laws).                             |     |       |\n   595\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   596\t| `dao.host.bytes`   | P: `bytes?`, `alloc` (fresh, zeroed), `length`, `get`, `slice` (fresh), `equal?`, `from-vector`      | 10  | H1    |\n   597\t|                    | (fresh), `to-vector`; M: `set!`, `copy!` (memmove). From `chunks.cljc:6-32`,                         |     |       |\n   598\t|                    | `jing/dht.cljc:100-121`, `linker.cljc:1232`, `sign.cljc:55-59`, `boring.cljc:46-51`,                 |     |       |\n   599\t|                    | `datagram.cljc:63-66`, `debruijn.cljc:167`. (`codec.cljc:45` reads it after the codec track's C4,    |     |       |\n   600\t|                    | §8.3.)                                                                                               |     |       |\n   601\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   602\t| `dao.host.text`    | P: `unit-count`, `code-unit`, `units->string`, `utf8-encode` (fresh bytes; refuses an unpaired       | 6   | H1    |\n   603\t|                    | surrogate), `utf8-decode` (refuses invalid sequences; never substitutes U+FFFD), `nfc` (Unicode      |     |       |\n   604\t|                    | 16.0) from `data.cljc:119-173`, `debruijn.cljc:241,310-321`, `jing.cljc:65-71,131-135`,              |     |       |\n   605\t|                    | `sign.cljc:62-66`.                                                                                   |     |       |\n   606\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   607\t| `dao.host.hash`    | P: `blake3-bytes`, `sha256-bytes` (`jing.cljc:59-135`; the string forms become portable over         | 2   | H3    |\n   608\t|                    | `text`).                                                                                             |     |       |\n   609\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   610\t| `dao.host.sign`    | P: `keypair-from-seed` (`sign.cljc:75-104`, seed replay), `sign`, `verify`. `generate` (fresh        | 3   | H3    |\n   611\t|                    | entropy, `:114-124`) stays in `yin.vm.linker.sign` until the deferred design moves it.               |     |       |\n   612\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   613\t| `dao.data.arrays`  | In place (OQ2). P: `anew` (fresh), `aget`, `alength`, `aclone` (fresh), `asub` (fresh), `aconcat`    | 12  | H2    |\n   614\t| (member by         | (fresh), `ainsert-at` (fresh), `aremove-at` (fresh), `from-coll` (fresh); M: `aset`, `acopy`         |     |       |\n   615\t| reference)         | (memmove), `asort` (stable; `parallelSort` replaced). `arrays.cljc:28-182`.                          |     |       |\n   616\t+--------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+-------+\n   617\t\n   618\t**Table B: portable over the profile, no host arm (P).** These functions\n   619\tcarry no reader arm and are **not counted in the 76**; two of them live in\n   620\t`dao.host.*` namespaces beside the arms they are built on. Base64 (replaces\n   621\t`goog.crypt.base64`, `dart:convert`, the JVM codec; **a replacement, not code\n   622\tmotion**; oracle V `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc`, 3 deftests:\n   623\t`rfc-4648-round-trips`, `decode-is-total-and-strict`, `every-length-round-trips`);\n   624\tthe Jing CBOR writer (replaces Boring and the Dart `cbor` package on the\n   625\tcontent path only, OQ4; a replacement; oracle table D); hex; `chunks/split`,\n   626\t`chunks/absorb`; and, added in r8 (R7-1), **built in H1**:\n   627\t\n   628\t- `dao.host.text/code-points` (P): the code points of a string as a vector\n   629\t  of integers, over `unit-count` and `code-unit`; a surrogate pair decodes\n   630\t  to one code point, an unpaired surrogate is its own code point. This is\n   631\t  the private `code-points` of `data.cljc:143-159` (V) made public and\n   632\t  moved; `yang/antlr/packet.cljc:64-69` (V: `.codePoints`, `.-runes`,\n   633\t  `js/Array.from`, which agree on paired and unpaired surrogates) switches\n   634\t  to it in H2. Oracle: the `data_test.cljc` code-point cases (table D) plus\n   635\t  `dao.host.text-test` cases for BMP, a non-BMP pair, a lone high and a\n   636\t  lone low surrogate, and the empty string.\n   637\t- `dao.host.float/decimal-text->float` (P): the double nearest to the\n   638\t  decimal text `digits[.digits]`, ties to even, by splitting the text into\n   639\t  its digit string and a base-10 exponent (minus the fraction length) and\n   640\t  calling `yin.vm.integer/decimal->float` (V `integer.cljc:769-776`, the\n   641\t  CPython `float(str)` algorithm, exported at `:855`; `yang` already\n   642\t  requires `yin.vm.integer`, V `yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc`). Law:\n   643\t  equals IEEE round-to-nearest-even of the exact decimal; answers `+inf`\n   644\t  past the double range and `0.0` below it, never a refusal for a\n   645\t  well-formed text; refuses a text that is not `digits[.digits]`. Oracle:\n   646\t  `integer_test.cljc` `float-text-named-cases-test` and\n   647\t  `int_contract_test.cljc` `float-rows-recompute-on-this-host` (V, through\n   648\t  `decimal->float`) plus `dao.host.float-test` cases for `\"1.5\"`, `\"0.1\"`,\n   649\t  `\"9007199254740993.0\"` (rounds to `9007199254740992.0`), a 400-digit\n   650\t  integer text (`+inf`), and `\"1.\"`. `yang/php.cljc:95-97` switches to it\n   651\t  in H2; since `Double/parseDouble`, `js/parseFloat` and Dart\n   652\t  `double.parse` are all nearest-even on this grammar (R), the float path\n   653\t  is not a behaviour change; the integer path at `:98-100` is (§10).\n   654\t\n   655\t**Table C: runtime prerequisites (documented and verified by existing\n   656\tsuites; not profile entries; not a boundary).**\n   657\t\n   658\t+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n   659\t| Prerequisite                     | Where, and the law a port must meet (V)                                                        | Slice   |\n   660\t+==================================+================================================================================================+=========+\n   760\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   761\t| Jing CBOR writer (table B)      | `test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json` with `cbor-v1.errata.md` preserved; `cbor_fixtures_test.cljc`    | V   |\n   762\t|                                 | (14 deftests), `cbor_conformance_test.cljc` (14): byte-identical production, `documented-skips-match-   |     |\n   763\t|                                 | the-errata-and-leave-no-case-unrun`; `cbor_test.cljc`; `jing_test.cljc`; `file_test.cljc` (17) replay.  |     |\n   764\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   765\t| base64 (table B)                | `test/dao/stream/base64_test.cljc` (3 deftests, named above).                                           | V   |\n   766\t+---------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----+\n   767\t\n   768\t### 4.4 The driver\n   769\t\n   770\tPer host, outside the core: the seam values of §4.1, clock readings as data,\n   771\tstdin/stdout, process exit, ambient facts as data. `yin.repl.main` is that\n   772\ttoday (V). Its deferred duties (entropy deposit, pump cadence) are §9's.\n   773\t\n   774\t### 4.5 Relation to the conformance kit and the wasm surface\n   775\t\n   776\t`yin.vm.engine.md` §E.5 presupposes a correct host value model. H1 supplies\n   777\t`dao.host.conformance-test` (table D through the new namespaces); E.5.2's\n   778\t\"R, owner, seal, profile and manifest addresses bit-identical\" is downstream\n   779\tof it. The stream-implementation suite is deferred (§9.4).\n   780\t\n   781\t## 5. What porting a host consists of (after H0-H4)\n   782\t\n   783\t1. Implement table A (76 functions) and meet table C for the dialect; green\n   784\t   `dao.host.conformance-test`. Hash and signature bind a library compiled\n   785\t   into the same instance.\n   786\t2. Load the adopted closure with a reader feature only where §3.3 syntax\n   787\t   requires it; the H0 gate proves zero source edits outside `dao.host.*`\n   788\t   and the §9 deferred files.\n   789\t3. The deferred seams (§9) remain per-host work until their design lands;\n   790\t   until then a port supplies them as today's hosts do, by reader arms in\n   791\t   the deferred files, which H0's allowlist permits.\n   792\t\n   793\t## 6. Verifiability\n   794\t\n   795\tByte-level oracles exist for every hot primitive (table D). H0's gate has\n   796\ttwo lists (files permitted non-exempt arms, §8.1; resolved effect calls\n   797\tpermitted) and two negative tests; it scans recursively and treats reading\n   798\tzero files as a failure distinct from zero matches, as does its library\n   799\tmode (§8.2) for the H2 and H3 host-library gates. Every H1-H4 acceptance is\n   800\tbyte-identical against a named corpus with errata preserved; the four\n   801\tbehaviour changes (§10) each have a direct test (table D).\n   802\t\n   803\t## 7. Consequence for wasm\n   804\t\n   805\tPrimitives execute in-instance. The import module `dao.stream` has exactly\n   806\tthe seven names of `dao.stream.wasm.md:38-46` (V); a primitive import is a\n   807\tboundary crossing and a violation of §2.2 whatever its purity. The gate that\n   808\tasserts a binary's import list is part of the deferred conformance suite\n   809\t(§9.4); until then the rule is stated here and checked by review.\n   810\t\n   811\t## 8. Slices H0-H4 (commissionable)\n   812\t\n   813\tExpand, migrate, contract. Each slice lands alone under the quick tier on\n   814\tthree lanes with recorded test and assertion counts; \"unchanged\" means equal\n   815\tcounts plus any added test named. The slow tier runs once after H4.\n   816\t\n   817\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   818\t| Slice | Phase  | Change                                                                         | Falsifiable acceptance                                            |\n   819\t+=======+========+================================================================================+===================================================================+\n   820\t| H0    | freeze | No `src/` change. (a) `src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (over                | Gate passes on the current tree; the committed closure output     |\n   821\t|       |        | `clojure.tools.namespace` parsing) and its output                              | lists exactly 142/140/141 files (§3.1) and the slice report       |\n   822\t|       |        | `docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn`, each file tagged with | records agreement with an independent traversal; the gate fails   |\n   823\t|       |        | its §3.1 class; (b) the gate test `dao.host.gate-test` over the closure with   | on one injected `#?(:clj` in a file outside list 1 and on one     |\n   824\t|       |        | **list 1** (files permitted non-exempt host arms, §8.1) and **list 2**         | injected `(random-uuid)` outside list 2 (two negative tests), and |\n   825\t|       |        | (resolved effect calls permitted: the §3.2 sites, plus the callers of M        | fails distinctly when it reads zero files (scan failure is not    |\n   826\t|       |        | entries named in §2.4), exempting §3.3 patterns; the gate scans files          | zero matches). Counts recorded.                                   |\n   827\t|       |        | recursively and fails if it read none; (c) per-lane counts; (d) the corpus     |                                                                   |\n   828\t|       |        | hash set.                                                                      |                                                                   |\n   829\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   830\t| H1    | expand | Create `dao.host.integer`, `.float`, `.number`, `.bytes`, `.text` with today's | Green; counts unchanged plus the named new tests; the new tests   |\n   850\t|       |        | change, §2.4); the M-entry callers of §2.4 are audited for the freeze rule.    | **Host-library gate (§8.2), built in this slice** as the library  |\n   851\t|       |        | The eight H0-found consumers (§3.1) migrate here as explicit **portability     | mode of `dao.host.gate-test`: within the adopted closure, no      |\n   852\t|       |        | corrections**: `bytes->str` over `text/utf8-decode` (encoding arity preserved, | executable reference to `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`,               |\n   853\t|       |        | OQ11), PHP literals over `integer/parse-decimal` and `decimal-text->float`,    | `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm` outside `dao/host/`;   |\n   854\t|       |        | the index comparator over `exact-integer?` plus `cbor/num-compare`, the packet | the H2 consumer tests of table D (`bytes->str`, PHP literals,     |\n   855\t|       |        | over `code-points`, the two safe-integer checks and three byte lengths. Then   | index signed zero) pass on three lanes; two negative tests: a     |\n   856\t|       |        | `yin.vm.integer.host` deleted; the shim mention in `integer.cljc:14` reworded. | fixture closure file holding an executable `BigInteger` reference |\n   857\t|       |        | Deliverable: the library mode of `dao.host.gate-test` with the H2 name list    | outside the allowlist fails the gate, and a fixture file naming   |\n   858\t|       |        | (§8.2).                                                                        | `BigInteger` only in a docstring and a keyword passes.            |\n   859\t|       |        |                                                                                | `yin.vm.engine` is touched (its require) and pinned by the engine |\n   860\t|       |        |                                                                                | suites. List 1 shrinks by the migrated files (§8.1).              |\n   861\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   862\t| H3    | expand | `dao.host.hash`, `dao.host.sign`; `dao.jing` and `yin.vm.linker.sign` require  | Green; counts unchanged plus `dao.host.hash-test`; every corpus   |\n   863\t|       | +migr. | them (`generate` stays, deferred). The string hash forms and `sign`'s `utf8`   | address identical; `sign_test` 4/4; `base64_test` 3/3 on three    |\n   864\t|       |        | switch to `text/utf8-encode`: a **named behaviour change** for strings with an | lanes; a direct test that `digest-string` and `message` refuse an |\n   865\t|       |        | unpaired surrogate (refusal instead of a substituted byte), recorded in the    | unpaired-surrogate string; **host-library gate (§8.2)**: within   |\n   866\t|       |        | slice report; such strings are already refused by the canonical codec (corpus  | the adopted closure, no executable reference to `MessageDigest`,  |\n   867\t|       |        | `unpaired-surrogate` class), so no persisted address changes. Base64 made      | `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,               |\n   868\t|       |        | portable (table B; a replacement).                                             | `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` outside `dao/host/`, and   |\n   869\t|       |        |                                                                                | for the Ed25519 names outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`           |\n   870\t|       |        |                                                                                | (`generate`); scan errors reported distinctly.                    |\n   871\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   872\t| H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\n   873\t|       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\n   874\t|       |        | the Dart `cbor` package for `dao.stream.cbor.cljd` (OQ4). A measurement:       | leave-no-case-unrun`); fixtures, DHT and linker image goldens     |\n   875\t|       |        | corpus and one large module image, old writer against new, JVM and Node.       | unchanged; the measurement in the slice report, no threshold      |\n   876\t|       |        |                                                                                | (OQ7). Slow tier once after landing.                              |\n   877\t+-------+--------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+\n   878\t\n   879\tDependencies: H0, H1, H2 in order; H3 and H4 after H2, in either order.\n   880\t\n   881\t### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\n   882\t\n   883\tThe gate never promises \"no arms across `src/cljc`\", only \"no non-exempt\n   884\tarms outside list 1\". List 1 is generated at H0 by the gate from the actual\n   885\tclosure (every closure file holding a non-exempt arm, §3.3) and must equal\n   886\tthe **H0 baseline** below, by category, with each file's reason; a\n   887\tdifference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1. The baseline\n   888\tis today's tree: the seven `dao.host.*` files are **planned additions**\n   889\t(five in H1, two in H3) and are not part of the H0 baseline; they are\n   890\tmarked as such in the table.\n   891\t\n   892\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   893\t| Category (reason)          | Files (V, from §1 and the closure)                                                              | After H4                    |\n   894\t+============================+=================================================================================================+=============================+\n   895\t| H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\n   896\t|                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (the Dart Jing writer; a lane-specific file counted here,    | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\n   897\t|                            | not under seams), `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,           | stays for `generate` only;  |\n   898\t|                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as  | three of these files are    |\n   899\t|                            | exempt protocol syntax), `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`,                    | deleted (§8.1 paragraph).   |\n   900\t|                            | `dao/jing/dht.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc` (bytes arms only); and,   |                             |\n   901\t|                            | from H0's finding (§3.1, profile consumers, H2): `yin/vm.cljc:404`, `dao/space/index.cljc:78`,  |                             |\n   902\t|                            | `yin/repl/query.cljc:460`, `yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc:32`, `yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:282`,         |                             |\n   903\t|                            | `yang/php.cljc:95,98`, `yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc:439`,                                |                             |\n   904\t|                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:130`, `yang/antlr/packet.cljc:67`.                       |                             |\n   905\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   906\t| Profile (the arms belong   | Baseline: `dao/data/arrays.cljc`. Planned additions, not in the H0 baseline:                    | Stay; the seven additions   |\n   907\t| here by design)            | `dao/host/{integer,float,number,bytes,text,hash,sign}.cljc` (P; five join list 1 at H1, two at  | are on list 1 from the      |\n   908\t|                            | H3).                                                                                            | slice that creates them.    |\n   909\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   910\t| Retained runtime           | `dao/data/btree.cljc` (atomic flag `:102-119`, weak and soft references `:212-245`: substantive | Stay, with the table C      |\n   911\t| prerequisites (table C)    | arms, not protocol syntax, retained by design); `dao/data/btree/storage.cljc` (promise facade,  | reason recorded in the      |\n   912\t|                            | deferred §9.1); `dao/pretty.cljc` (`StringWriter`/pprint, display only, §3.1).                  | gate's list.                |\n   913\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   914\t| Codec-track files          | `dao/stream/ws.cljc`, `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`. (H0:       | Stay; owned by that track;  |\n   915\t| (untouched by this track)  | `remote_channel.cljc` and `ws_project.cljc` carry only exempt `catch` arms and are not on the   | `codec.cljc:45` after C4.   |\n   916\t|                            | generated list; `jing/stream.cljc` is not in the closure. All three remain codec-track files    |                             |\n   917\t|                            | under §8.3; they are simply not list-1 entries.)                                                |                             |\n   918\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   919\t| Dialect arms (H0 finding,  | `dao/space/query.cljc` (`:808`), `yang/clojure.cljc` (`:375`), `yin/vm/engine.cljc` (`:929`): a | Stay.                       |\n   920\t| retained)                  | runtime type name in diagnostic text; `yin/repl/adapter.cljc` (`:58`), `yin/repl/dht.cljc`      |                             |\n   921\t|                            | (`:104`): the dialect's EDN reader under two namespaces. Five files.                            |                             |\n   922\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   923\t| Seams, stream              | `src/clj`, `src/cljs`, `src/cljd` seam and shadow files (§3.1 lane-specific list) **except**    | Stay, except the Dart Jing  |\n   924\t| implementations and driver | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`, which is a Jing writer H4 deletes, not a seam; it is on the | writer, deleted in H4.      |\n   925\t|                            | baseline under the first row's `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` twin. `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc`   |                             |\n   926\t|                            | (`:168`, the in-memory stream implementation's own host atom test: an                           |                             |\n   927\t|                            | **implementation-private** arm under §4.1, its one name in this document and in the closure     |                             |\n   928\t|                            | class `:external-stream-seam`). `yin/repl/main.cljc`, `yin/repl/host.cljc`,                     |                             |\n   929\t|                            | `yin/repl/state.cljc`.                                                                          |                             |\n   930\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   931\t| Deferred-scope files (§9)  | `dao/jing/file.cljc`, `dao/space/store/fs.cljc`, `dao/space/store.cljc`,                        | Stay until the deferred     |\n   932\t|                            | `dao/stream/journal/file.cljc`, `dao/jing/coordinate.cljc`, `dao/space/dht.cljc`,               | design lands.               |\n   933\t|                            | `dao/stream/rpc.cljc` (`:114`, the `rand` arm), `yin/repl.cljc`,                                |                             |\n   934\t|                            | `yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc` and the other `yang/python/antlr/*.cljc` with arms,             |                             |\n   935\t|                            | `dao/stream/journal.cljc` (`locking`), `dao/space/transactor.cljc`, `yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc` |                             |\n   936\t|                            | (`locking`). (H0: `dao/jing/content/ async.cljc`, `dao/stream/udp.cljc` and                     |                             |\n   937\t|                            | `dao/space/schema.cljc` are not in the closure and are dropped from list 1; the deferred design |                             |\n   938\t|                            | records them, §9.) Every remaining closure file whose arms are only `catch`/hint/protocol       |                             |\n   939\t|                            | syntax is **not** on list 1 (exempt by pattern).                                                |                             |\n   940\t+----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\n   941\t\n   942\t**Baseline versus additions and deletions.** The H0 baseline is the set of\n   943\t**existing** files above (every entry except the planned additions named\n   944\tin the profile row). The planned additions are the seven `dao/host/*.cljc`\n   945\tfiles (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\n   946\tthree: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\n   947\tJVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\n   948\tJing writer, a lane-specific file that the seams row excludes and the first\n   949\trow lists, so that the lane-specific category cannot silently retain it).\n   950\tThe final list 1 after H4 is therefore: the baseline minus the first row\n   951\t(except `sign.cljc` for `generate`), both deleted Jing writers included in\n   952\tthat subtraction, plus the seven profile files. The host-library gate of\n   953\t§8.2 is consistent with it.\n   954\t\n   955\t**Reconciliation with H0's measurement (r7, V).** H0 generated list 1 as\n   956\t76 files: 60 matching the rows above after the corrections now in them,\n   957\tplus 16 tagged `:h0-unlisted`. The 16 are now categorised: nine in the\n   958\tfirst row (profile consumers, H2), five in the \"dialect arms\" row\n   959\t(retained), one (`ringbuffer.cljc`) in the seams row, one (`rpc.cljc`) in\n   960\tthe deferred row. **Two vocabularies, kept distinct (R7-4)**: a **closure\n   961\tclass** (the `:classes` set on each file in the committed edn, generated\n   962\tfrom the `class-rows` data in `closure.clj:112`, V) answers \"what host\n   963\tcontact does this file have\" per §3.1; a **gate category** (the\n   964\t`list-1-categories` of `gate_test.clj:444`, V) answers \"why is this file\n   965\tpermitted a non-exempt arm\" per §8.1. The mapping is many-to-one and the\n   966\tgate test asserts it. **What H0 must change**: edit the classification\n   967\t**data** (the `class-rows` of `closure.clj`, which the worktree already\n   968\textends with `:profile-consumer` and `:dialect-arm`, and the gate's list 1\n   969\tcategories) so that no entry is `:h0-unlisted`, then regenerate the edn\n   970\toutputs; drop nothing (the six names H0 could not find were never on the\n   971\tgenerated list, and the rows above no longer name them). **What H0 must\n   972\tnot change**: the traversal algorithm and its resolution rule, the totals\n   973\t142/140/141 and 133 shared, the independent-traversal agreement, the two\n   974\tnegative tests' semantics, the scan-failure test and the corpus hash set;\n   975\tthe lanes need not be re-run beyond `dao.host.gate-test` and the tool's\n   976\t`--check`. **How H1 and H2 clear\n   977\tthe tag**: H1 adds no consumer, so the nine stay tagged `:migration-source`;\n   978\tH2 migrates them with the other consumers and removes them from list 1 in\n   979\tthe same commit, which the `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms` test enforces.\n   980\tThe tool lives at `src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj` (H0's justified\n   981\tdeviation: the repo keeps dev tools under `src/dev/`), and the design's\n   982\tearlier `dev/host_boundary/` path is read as that.\n   983\t\n   984\t### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\n   985\t\n   986\tA literal `grep` over `src/cljc` is **not** the gate: it matches a docstring\n   987\tin the untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` (\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\", V) and the\n   988\tout-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`:rgba8unorm`, V), so\n   989\tits asserted result would be false. The gate is instead `dao.host.gate-test`\n   990\trun in **library mode**, which **lands with H2**, not H0: H0 is a freeze\n   991\twith no source change and the library mode has no consumer before H2's\n   992\tdeletion, so building it in H0 would add a deliverable nothing exercises\n   993\tand nothing can falsify; H2 builds it with the H2 name list and its two\n   994\tnegative tests (below), and H3 extends the name list. In library mode the\n   995\tgate takes the H0 closure tool's tagged file list\n   996\tfor the adopted closure (so out-of-scope files never count), reads each\n   997\tfile with the Clojure reader per lane feature (so comments and string\n   998\tliterals, docstrings included, never count), and collects symbols, class\n   999\tnames and import/require forms; a hit is any such symbol naming\n  1000\t`BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`, `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm`\n  1150\tdecodes UTF-8 **with U+FFFD substitution for malformed input** (V\n  1151\t`vm.cljc:404-408`; `String.` with a charset replaces malformed sequences),\n  1152\tso non-ASCII bytes change on JS and Dart and malformed bytes change on all\n  1153\tthree; (4) PHP integer literals above 2^53 become exact on JS (H2). The\n  1154\t`aset` return value is kept as Clojure's: unchanged, stated only so the law\n  1155\tcannot be read as changing it. H1 medium: new namespaces plus two new laws,\n  1156\ttwo table B functions and their tests.\n  1157\tH2 medium: seventeen consumers (nine of r5 plus the eight H0 found, two of\n  1158\tthem with named behaviour changes, §3.1), the Jing carrier move, the arrays\n  1159\tprevalidation change and the M-caller audit in one slice; mitigated by the corpus, the\n  1160\tpre-deletion closure-tool gate and splitting the slice per namespace if the report\n  1161\tshows drift. H3 low-to-medium: the UTF-8 behaviour change is observable only\n  1162\ton unpaired-surrogate strings, which the codec already refuses. H4\n  1163\tlow-to-medium: the corpus decides; performance unknown until measured. The\n  1164\tClojureDart traps are named in §14.\n  1165\t\n  1166\tReversal: an owner ruling that reader arms are the intended port mechanism;\n  1167\ta measured H4 regression that matters (the portable writer stays as oracle\n  1168\tand a host supplies a faster one behind the same profile); owner rejection\n  1169\tof §12 (then §2 stands as this document's reading of the existing ABI text).\n  1170\t\n  1171\t## 11. Decision record\n  1172\t\n  1173\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1174\t| Id   | Decision                                                                                                         | Status                       |\n  1175\t+======+==================================================================================================================+==============================+\n  1176\t| HD1  | The governing test: dao.stream wherever the contact can be an IO action with respect to the world (§2.1-2.3); an | Owner rule (\"test 2          |\n  1177\t|      | internal pure, total, synchronous function, or a declared mutation of an owned argument, may be a direct call.   | governs\"); r3 wording needs  |\n  1178\t|      |                                                                                                                  | non-Claude sign-off          |\n  1179\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1180\t| HD2  | Internal contacts form the primitive profile: 76 entries (§4.2 table A) with kinds P/M and the §2.4 ownership    | Architect r3; needs sign-off |\n  1181\t|      | laws, plus runtime prerequisites (table C); in-instance for wasm (§7).                                           |                              |\n  1182\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1183\t| HD3  | Commissionable scope is §2 plus H0-H4; entropy, scheduling, storage, parser stage and stream conformance are     | Owner, 2026-10-20 (\"yes,     |\n  1184\t|      | deferred to a separate design with the §9 required inputs.                                                       | proceed with the split\")     |\n  1185\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1186\t| HD4  | H0 gates both reader arms and resolved effect calls over the committed per-lane closure; list 1 names retained   | Architect r3