 OQ1  | Scope is the `yin.repl` closure; GUI, graphics and demo namespaces excluded.                                     | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1205\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1206\t| OQ2  | The profile family is `dao.host.*`; `dao.data.arrays` stays in place as a profile member by reference.           | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1207\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1208\t| OQ3  | Arm-adding work in the files H1-H3 touch is paused until phase A lands; boundary-agnostic probes proceed.        | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1209\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1210\t| OQ4  | Boring and the Dart `cbor` package are dropped from the Jing content path only; the transport codec keeps them.  | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1211\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1212\t| OQ5  | Storage is a seam beneath the journal, not a streams-all-the-way-down redesign (now deferred, §9.2).             | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1213\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1214\t| OQ6  | This track has its own orchestrator seat, independent of the codec track and any host-lane track.                | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1215\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1216\t| Spli | Commissionable scope is the rule plus H0-H4; the rest is deferred to a separate design.                          | Owner, 2026-10-20            |\n  1217\t| t    |                                                                                                                  |                              |\n  1218\t+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+\n  1219\t\n  1220\t## 12. OWNER PROPOSAL: amendment to datom.world.abi.md (not doctrine; not applied)\n  1221\t\n  1222\tThis section is a proposal for the owner's approval (OQ8). It is **not**\n  1223\tverbatim doctrine and nothing in `datom.world.abi.md` or `datom.world.md`\n  1224\thas been edited. The owner's quoted words are marked as such; the rest is\n  1225\tthe Architect's proposed wording, to be revised by the owner.\n  1226\t\n  1227\t**12.1 Proposed new §8 of `datom.world.abi.md`, \"The governing test\".**\n  1228\t\n  1229\t> Owner ruling, 2026-10-20 (verbatim): \"when the host boundary can be an IO\n  1230\t> monad then dao.stream is used. If it cannot be a monad than dao.stream\n  1300\t\n  1301\tStart with **H0**: it changes no source; commit the closure tool\n  1302\t(`src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj`, over `clojure.tools.namespace`), its\n  1303\tper-lane output under `docs/design/host-boundary/` tagged by class, and the\n  1304\tgate test; confirm the 142/140/141 totals against an independent traversal\n  1305\t(done, H0 report) and finish the r7 reconciliation of list 1 (§8.1: retag\n  1306\tthe 16 `:h0-unlisted` entries, a data change only) before H1; a non-Claude\n  1307\treviewer confirms r7 and the retagged H0 before H1 is dispatched. Then H1 (new files,\n  1308\ttheir direct tests, and the two new laws: strict `utf8-encode` and M-entry\n  1309\tprevalidation). H2 is the first deletion; its gate is the closure tool\n  1310\treading `ns` forms (the shim required by no file before the deletion commit,\n  1311\tabsent and required by no file after), and it carries the\n  1312\t`acopy` prevalidation change and the M-caller audit (§2.4). H3 carries the\n  1313\tnamed UTF-8 behaviour change for its two consumers. H3 and H4 in either\n  1314\torder; slow tier once after H4. Do not start anything in §9; a separate\n  1315\tdesign document and its own non-Claude sign-off come first.\n  1316\t\n  1317\tLanes and gates (`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`): iterate on the JVM lane\n  1318\twith `bb test:sub:clj dao.jing` or `yin.vm` (G0); three-lane subsystem test\n  1319\tat each checkpoint (G1); `bb test:changed` across all three lanes in the\n  1320\tworktree before landing (G2); `bb test` on master after merge (G3). Record\n  1321\tper-lane counts before and after every slice. The Dart lane needs `flutter`\n  1322\ton PATH; a fresh worktree needs `npm ci`. ClojureDart traps for exactly this\n  1323\tkind of file: `:cljd` first in every mixed conditional; a tail-position\n  1324\t`:cljd nil` silently fails; protocol method parameters never `[_ _]`;\n  1325\t`(- 0.0)` is `+0.0`; multi-key `assoc` on nil misbehaves.\n  1326\t\n  1327\tReview requirement: this design and any implementation an orchestrator\n  1328\tderives from it under a Claude model are Claude-authored. **Sign-off on this\n  1329\tfinal text (§2 plus H0-H4) and on each slice must come from a non-Claude\n  1330\tarchitect**; a Claude reviewer may review but may not be the sole sign-off.\n  1331\tThe reviewer checks, in order: that every entry in table A is internal and\n  1332\tpure or declared mutating under §2.4, with the freeze rule's enforceable\n  1333\tobligations (i)-(iv) each backed by a test or an audited list; that H0's\n  1334\tcommitted closure output matches 142/140/141 and list 1 matches the §8.1\n  1335\tbaseline by category; that the two negative tests and the scan-failure test\n  1336\tfail as intended; that H2's closure-tool gates hold before and after the deletion\n  1337\tcommit and the no-partial-write tests exist; that H1-H4 acceptance is\n  1338\tbyte-identical against the named corpus with errata preserved and the four\n  1339\tbehaviour changes are named in slice reports with their table D tests; that\n  1340\tthe `bytes->str` encoding arity is preserved until OQ11 is decided; that\n  1341\tthe index comparator keeps signed zero and NaN order (R7-3); that no H0-H4 edit touches a\n  1342\tcodec-track source or test file except the recorded `codec.cljc:45` deferral;\n  1343\tthat nothing from §9 is started.\n  1344\t\n  1345\t## Appendix A. Citations opened for this document (2026-10-20, read only)\n  1346\t\n  1347\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1348\t| Cite                                                         | Finding                                                                                          |\n  1349\t+==============================================================+==================================================================================================+\n  1350\t| `docs/design/datom.world.md:16-32,43-48,68-71`               | Axioms; side effects as emissions; the sentence §12.2 proposes to change.                        |\n  1351\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1352\t| `docs/design/datom.world.abi.md:21-24,35-44,47-52,56-64,`    | One ABI; custody; machine-internal work in-instance; the floor and internal linkage; effects     |\n  1353\t| `75-87,94-148`                                               | out, events in; adapter discipline; the two non-adapters.                                        |\n  1354\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1355\t| `docs/design/dao.stream.wasm.md:29-52`                       | Seven imports; primitives have no imports.                                                       |\n  1356\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1357\t| `docs/design/dao.stream.codec.md:140-180,658-780`            | Contract namespace; slice file set; the 22 test namespaces (§8.3).                               |\n  1358\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1359\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc:1-298`                    | 25 public functions; \"depends on nothing\".                                                       |\n  1360\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1361\t| `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:1-101`; `yin/vm.cljc:32,929`;  | Consumers of the shim (requires and `big-carrier?` sites).                                       |\n  1362\t| `yin/vm/engine.cljc:38,810`; `yin/vm/values.cljc:30,196`;    |                                                                                                  |\n  1363\t| `yin/vm/data.cljc:41,421,547`; `test/yang/python/antlr/`     |                                                                                                  |\n  1364\t| `{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test.cljc`                   |                                                                                                  |\n  1365\t+--------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  1366\t| `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:1-60,95-254,342-460,483-632,`   | Rea