 deleted; the shim mention in `integer.cljc:14` reworded. | fixture closure file holding an executable `BigInteger` reference |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:872:| H4    | migr.  | Portable Jing CBOR writer over `dao.host.*`; `dao.jing.cbor.boring` and        | Green; `cbor-v1.json` byte-identical on three lanes with the      |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:873:|       |        | `dao.jing.cbor.cljd` deleted; Boring stays for `dao.stream.cbor.boring` and    | errata skips unchanged (`documented-skips-match-the-errata-and-   |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:895:| H1-H4 migration sources    | `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,                  | Removed from list 1 as each |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:896:|                            | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (the Dart Jing writer; a lane-specific file counted here,    | slice lands; `sign.cljc`    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:898:|                            | `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc` (table C blocks stay, as  | three of these files are    |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:924:| implementations and driver | `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`, which is a Jing writer H4 deletes, not a seam; it is on the | writer, deleted in H4.      |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:925:|                            | baseline under the first row's `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` twin. `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc`   |                             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:946:three: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:947:JVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1019:H0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1020:`dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1022:`yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1023:`yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1030:H0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1031:`yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1033:`yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1038:and `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1134:(`yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1135:`src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`), **7** `dao.host.*` files added (five in\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1298:and `dao.host.float/decimal-text->float` with their tests (table D); the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1359:| `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc:1-298`                    | 25 public functions; \"depends on nothing\".                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1361:| `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:1-101`; `yin/vm.cljc:32,929`;  | Consumers of the shim (requires and `big-carrier?` sites).                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1363:| `yin/vm/data.cljc:41,421,547`; `test/yang/python/antlr/`     |                                                                                                  |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1366:| `src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:1-60,95-254,342-460,483-632,`   | Reader; big-integer helpers; carriers with equality and hash; JVM Decimal/Ratio construction and |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1401:| `test/yin/vm/integer_v3_fixtures.cljc`;                      |                                                                                                  |\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:28:            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:32:            [yin.vm.integer.host :as integer-host]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1075:   `dao.jing.cbor/content=`, the encoder's own kind-strict equality, so canonical\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1128:   leaves by `dao.jing.cbor/content=`), and a mismatch throws\n        A real token's text is the source at its span.\n     5. A rule's span covers its real children only; an empty rule is\n        zero-width.\n     6. Any syntax error yields an error packet with :yang.cst/errors and no\n        nodes.\n     7. :yang.cst/grammar names the grammar revision and tool; the target does\n        not appear in the packet. Target equivalence is the contract.\n\n   Portable and language-agnostic: child edges are data, so the tree is\n   validated before anything walks it.\")\n\n\n(def packet-version 1)\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Source text\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn code-points\n  \"The code points of `s` as a vector of integers.\"\n  [s]\n  #?(:cljd (vec (.-runes ^String s))\n     :clj (mapv long (.toArray (.codePoints ^String s)))\n     :cljs (mapv #(.codePointAt % 0) (js/Array.from s))))\n\n\n(defn utf8-length\n(ns yang.php\n  \"Yang PHP compiler - Compiles PHP code into Yin VM Universal AST.\n\n  Supports:\n  - Function definitions (named and anonymous)\n  - Closures with 'use' clauses\n  - Conditionals (if/elseif/else)\n  - Variables ($name)\n  - Assignments ($x = val) and Augmented Assignments ($x *= val)\n  - Post-increment ($x++)\n  - For loops (desugared to recursive lambdas)\n  - Basic operators and literals\n  - Semicolon-terminated statements\n  - Braced blocks\n  - Type hints (parsed and ignored)\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile])\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\n\n\n;; Forward declarations\n(declare compile-stmt\n         parse-php-expr\n         parse-php-statement\n         parse-php-block\n         parse-php-primary)\n\n\n;; ============================================================================\n;; PHP Tokenizer\n;; ============================================================================\n\n(defn tokenize\n  \"Tokenize PHP source code.\"\n  [source]\n  (loop [s (str/trim source)\n         tokens []]\n    (if (empty? s)\n      tokens\n      (let\n        [patterns\n         [[:number #\"^\\d+\\.?\\d*\"] [:string #\"^\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"\"]\n          [:string #\"^'([^']*)'\"]\n          [:keyword\n           #\"^(function|return|if|else|elseif|true|false|null|use|for|int|float|string|bool|void|mixed|array|object)\\b\"]\n          [:variable #\"^\\$[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\"]\n          [:identifier #\"^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*\"]\n          [:operator\n           #\"^(==|!=|<=|>=|<|>|\\+\\+|\\-\\-|\\+=|\\-=|\\*=|/=|\\+|-|\\*|/|&&|\\|\\||!|=)\"]\n          [:lparen #\"^\\(\"] [:rparen #\"^\\)\"] [:lbrace #\"^\\{\"] [:rbrace #\"^\\}\"]\n          [:comma #\"^,\"] [:semicolon #\"^;\"] [:colon #\"^:\"]\n          [:whitespace #\"^[ \\t\\n\\r]+\"]]\n         matched\n         (some (fn [[type pattern]]\n                 (when-let [match (re-find pattern s)]\n                   (let [full-match (if (string? match) match (first match))\n                         value\n                         (if (= type :string) (second match) full-match)]\n                     {:type type, :value value, :length (count full-match)})))\n               patterns)]\n        (if matched\n          (recur (subs s (:length matched))\n                 (if (= :whitespace (:type matched))\n                   tokens\n                   (conj tokens [(:type matched) (:value matched)])))\n          (cond (str/starts-with? s \"<?php\") (recur (subs s 5) tokens)\n                (str/starts-with? s \"?>\") (recur (subs s 2) tokens)\n                :else (throw (ex-info \"Tokenization error\"\n                                      {:remaining\n                                       (subs s 0 (min 20 (count s)))}))))))))\n\n\n;; ============================================================================\n;; PHP Parser\n;; ============================================================================\n    (is (= 1 (call 'compare-float (call 'neg (call 'shift-left 1 5000))\n                   ninf)))))\n\n\n(deftest float-text-named-cases-test\n  (is (= [\"7120236347223045\" -307]\n         (call 'float-digits (fx/bits->double \"0060000000000000\")))\n      \"2^-1017: the interval below a power of two is the narrow one\")\n  (is (= [\"6189700196426902\" 26]\n         (call 'float-digits (fx/bits->double \"4580000000000000\"))))\n  (is (= [\"5\" -324] (call 'float-digits (fx/bits->double \"0000000000000001\"))))\n  (is (= \"7fefffffffffffff\"\n         (fx/double->bits\n           (call 'decimal->float\n                 (call 'format (call 'sub (call 'shift-left 1 1024)\n                                     (call 'shift-left 1 971)))\n                 0)))\n      \"the largest double, 2^1024 - 2^971, reads back exactly\")\n  (is (= (refused 'float-digits :wrong-type\n                  {::integer/arg 0, ::integer/expected :finite-nonzero-float})\n         (refusal call 'float-digits (fx/bits->double \"0000000000000000\"))))\n  (is (= 4300 (call 'max-digits))))\n\n\n(deftest float-refusals-test\n  (is (= (refused 'true-div :zero-division {}) (refusal call 'true-div 1 0)))\n  (is (= (refused 'true-div :zero-division {})\n         (refusal call 'true-div (big two-64) (big \"0\"))))\n  (is (= (refused 'to-float :wrong-type {::integer/arg 0,\n                                         ::integer/expected :integer})\n         (refusal call 'to-float 0.5)))\n  (is (= (refused 'compare-float :wrong-type {::integer/arg 1,\n                                              ::integer/expected :float})\n         (refusal call 'compare-float 1 \"1\")))\n  (is (= (refused 'compare-float :wrong-type\n                  {::integer/arg 1, ::integer/expected :non-nan-float})\n         (refusal call 'compare-float 1 (fx/bits->double \"7ff8000000000000\"))))\n  (doseq [x [\"7ff8000000000000\" \"7ff0000000000000\" \"fff0000000000000\"]]\n    (is (= (refused 'from-float :wrong-type\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Each row, recomputed on this host\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest integer-rows-recompute-on-this-host\n  (doseq [s f/int-names\n          [c text] (f/int-rows s)]\n    (is (= (f/column @fixture s c) text) (str s \" \" c))))\n\n\n(deftest float-rows-recompute-on-this-host\n  (doseq [s f/float-names\n          [c text] (f/float-rows s)]\n    (is (= (f/column @fixture s c) text) (str s \" \" c))))\n\n\n(deftest text-round-trips-through-the-module\n  (testing \"parse of the frozen decimal and hex text gives back the value:\n            its canonical bytes are the frozen bytes\"\n    (doseq [s f/int-names]\n      (let [cbor (f/column @fixture s \"cbor\")]\n        (is (= cbor (f/cbor-hex (f/call (f/module 100000 100000) 'parse\n                                        (f/column @fixture s \"dec\"))))\n            (str s \" dec\"))\n        (is (= cbor (f/cbor-hex (f/call (f/module 100000 100000) 'parse\n                                        (f/column @fixture s \"hex\") 16)))\n|      |                                                                                                      | reading.                                           |\n+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n| OQ11 | The public encoding arity of the yin primitive `bytes->str` (`yin/vm.cljc:403-409`, V): today a      | Make it portable: accept `\"UTF-8\"` (any case)      |\n|      | JVM-only two-arity `[b enc]` that decodes with any Java charset; JS and Dart have the one-arity      | through `utf8-decode`, answer a qualified refusal  |\n|      | only, so a guest program using it runs on one host. Remove it, keep it JVM-only, or make it portable | for any other name on every host. Evidence: no     |\n|      | with UTF-8 the only accepted name? Not decided here (review R7-2: absence of repository callers does | caller in `src` or `test` (V, grep); the macro     |\n|      | not establish compatibility for a public primitive). Until decided, H2 preserves the arity as it is  | prelude excludes it (`macro.cljc:666`, V); a       |\n|      | on the JVM, behind a retained arm on list 1.                                                         | one-host primitive contradicts the universal AST.  |\n+------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+\n\nOQ1-OQ6 are closed (§11.1). OQ9 and OQ10 belong to the deferred design\n(§9.1). OQ11 does not block H1; H2 preserves the arity until it is decided.\n\n## 14. For a successor orchestrator\n\nDecided (HD1-HD5, OQ1-OQ6, the split): the rule, the exact profile with\nownership laws, the H0-H4 sequence and gates, the deferral. Open: OQ7, OQ8,\n30:  (:require\n143:  \"The namespaces an ns form requires on a lane: :require, :use and\n144:   :require-macros clauses.\"\n149:         (filter #(#{:require :use :require-macros} (first %)))\n214:      (some #(= 'ns (head %)) ancestors) :ns-require-arm\n330:                   (filter #(#{:require :use} (first %)))\n444:(def list-1-categories\n465:(def list-1\n630:(defn gate\n633:  [sources list-1 list-2]\n638:                                  :when (and (seq (:arms r)) (not (contains? list-1 f)))]\n664:  (delay (gate (read-sources (closure-files)) list-1 list-2)))\n702:(deftest list-1-equals-the-observed-arms\n703:  (testing \"every list-1 file is in the closure and still holds a host arm\"\n705:      (is (= (set (keys list-1)) observed))))\n706:  (testing \"every list-1 file has an explained §8.1 category and a clearing slice\"\n707:    (doseq [[f {:keys [category clears]}] list-1]\n708:      (is (contains? list-1-categories category) (str f \" \" category))\n709:      (is (contains? (get-in list-1-categories [category :clears]) clears)\n713:      (doseq [f (keys list-1)]\n735:(deftest an-injected-host-arm-outside-list-1-fails-the-gate\n736:  (let [target (outside list-1)\n739:        r (gate sources list-1 list-2)]\n750:        r (gate sources list-1 list-2)]\n760:    (let [r (gate {} list-1 list-2)]\n765:                  list-1 list-2)]\n794:    (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \"(ns a (:require #?(:clj [x :as y] :cljs [z :as y])))\"))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
