{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '670,686p' docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md; sed -n '24,46p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; sed -n '60,72p' src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc; sed -n '450,465p' src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc; sed -n '25,38p' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc; sed -n '275,290p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '433,446p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc; sed -n '125,137p' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc; sed -n '803,813p' src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc; sed -n '370,380p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc; sed -n '923,935p' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc; sed -n '53,63p' src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc; sed -n '99,109p' src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc; sed -n '163,175p' src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc; sed -n '109,120p' src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| `locking`, atoms, volatiles      | Five `locking` sites (§3.1); single-owner discipline elsewhere.                                | none    |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Host promise type                | `btree/storage.cljc:218-227`: deferred (§9.1).                                                 | defer   |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n| Dialect syntax                   | §3.3.                                                                                          | H0      |\n+----------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+---------+\n\nLayering: `dao.host.*` requires nothing in the repo; `dao` never requires\n`yin`. Consumers after H2: `dao.jing`, `dao.jing.cbor`, `yin.vm.integer`,\n`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.values`, `yin.vm.engine`, `yin.vm`, `yin.vm.debruijn`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn-code`, `dao.stream.chunks`, `dao.jing.dht`, `yin.vm.linker`,\n`yin.vm.linker.sign`, `dao.stream.datagram`, `dao.stream.base64`, and the\nthree Python integer tests.\n\n### 4.3 Oracle coverage matrix (table D)\n\n   - **`call-in-cursor-key` is dropped.** v1 wrote it and nothing read it.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [eval])\n  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.space.query :as query]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yin.vm.effect :as effect]\n            [yin.vm.integer.host :as integer-host]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Protocols\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Common VM interfaces implemented by all execution engines.\n\n(defprotocol IVM\n  \"Unified VM protocol for execution, evaluation, and observable state.\"\n\n  (step\n    [vm]\n    \"Execute one step of already-loaded work. An idle VM is returned\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Source text\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn code-points\n  \"The code points of `s` as a vector of integers.\"\n  [s]\n  #?(:cljd (vec (.-runes ^String s))\n     :clj (mapv long (.toArray (.codePoints ^String s)))\n     :cljs (mapv #(.codePointAt % 0) (js/Array.from s))))\n\n\n(defn utf8-length\n                            :else (str \"a program was refused (\"\n                                       (name (or (:reason failure)\n                                                 (:stage failure)))\n                                       \")\"))\n                      \"; (reset) rebuilds them\")\n                 nil)))))\n\n\n(defn- byte-length\n  [bs]\n  #?(:cljd (.-length ^Uint8List bs)\n     :default (alength bs)))\n\n\n(defn- encoded-size\n  \"The canonical CBOR size of `x`, or nil when `x` is not portable data.\"\n  [[:yin.semantic/code linker/semantic-format]\n   [:yin.debruijn.code linker/stack-format]\n   [:yin.debruijn.register linker/register-format]])\n\n\n(defn- byte-count\n  [bs]\n  #?(:cljd (.-length ^typed/Uint8List bs)\n     :clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n     :cljs (.-length bs)))\n\n\n(defn- stop\n  \"`st` ended by the terminal `outcome`.\"\n            (work! ctx total))\n        (let [s (first stack) stack (rest stack)]\n          (if (empty? s)\n            (recur stack total steps)\n            (let [x (first s)\n                  stack (cons (rest s) stack)\n                  total (+ total (cond\n                                   (cbor/byte-payload? x) (+ 16 #?(:cljd (.-length x) :default (alength x)))\n                                   (string? x) (+ 128 (* 4 (count x)))\n                                   (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) (+ 128 (* 4 (count (str x))))\n                                   :else 128))]\n              (if (> total remaining)\n                (do (swap! counter update :estimator-steps (fnil + 0) (inc steps))\n                    (work! ctx total))\n                (recur (cond->> stack\n                         (coll? x) (cons (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) (seq x)))\n        (range (count instructions))))\n\n\n(defn- nonneg-int?\n  [x]\n  (and (integer? x) (not (neg? x))\n       #?(:cljs (js/Number.isSafeInteger x) :default true)))\n\n\n(def ^:private operand-kind-checks\n  {:reg nonneg-int?,\n   :uint nonneg-int?,\n   :regs (fn [x] (and (vector? x) (every? nonneg-int? x))),\n   :str string?,\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- nonneg-int?\n  [x]\n  (and (integer? x) (not (neg? x))\n       #?(:cljs (js/Number.isSafeInteger x) :default true)))\n\n\n(defn- ascending-distinct?\n  [xs]\n  (every? (fn [[a b]] (< a b)) (partition 2 1 xs)))\n\n\n;; q: Datalog (:find / :in / :where over bounded db streams)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- type-label\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n     :default (str (type x))))\n\n\n(defn- content-eq\n  \"The query `=`: kind-strict content equality (dao.jing.cbor/content=),\n          ;; Function application: (f arg1 arg2 ...)\n          (compile-application operator operands env tail? macro-env))))\n    ;; Unknown form type\n    :else (throw (ex-info \"Cannot compile unknown form type\"\n                          {:form form,\n                           :type #?(:cljd (clojure.core/str (.-runtimeType form))\n                                    :default (clojure.core/type form))}))))\n\n\n(defn compile-form\n  \"Compile one Clojure form and retain the reader's plain metadata on the\n              (vector? x) (mapv encode x)\n              (set? x) (into #{} (map encode) x)\n              (seq? x) (apply list (map encode x))\n              (fn? x) (encode-primitive vm x)\n              :else (non-portable! :host-object\n                                   {:yin.k/hint\n                                    #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n                                       :default (str (type x)))})))]\n    encode))\n\n\n(defn- decoder\n  \"UCF 7.5.1's `decode` into `vm`'s coordinates: every map is a marker, a\n(defn- read-forms\n  \"Read the line with a non-evaluating reader on every host.  Sniffing an input\n   line for a shell command must never run it; anything the data reader rejects\n   is ordinary source for the remote evaluator.\"\n  [input]\n  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n     :clj (edn/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))\n     :cljs (reader/read-string (str \"[\" input \"]\"))))\n\n\n(defn command-form\n;; heads.edn (5.7)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- read-edn\n  [text]\n  #?(:cljd (edn/read-string text)\n     :clj (edn/read-string text)\n     :cljs (reader/read-string text)))\n\n\n(defn- read-one\n(defn- resolve-state\n  [resolver identity]\n  (let [x (if (fn? resolver) (resolver identity) (get resolver identity))]\n    (cond (instance? RingHandle x) (.-state ^RingHandle x)\n          #?(:cljd false\n             :clj (instance? clojure.lang.IAtom x)\n             :cljs (instance? cljs.core/Atom x)) x\n          :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn attach!\n  \"Attach using a host-owned resolver (identity -> handle/state).\"\n  [resolver descriptor]\n;; Explicit client state\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- random-safe-id\n  []\n  #?(:clj (long (* max-safe-id (rand)))\n     :cljs (Math/floor (* max-safe-id (rand)))\n     :cljd (.floor ^double (* max-safe-id (rand)))))\n\n\n(defn client-state\n  \"Create caller-owned RPC client state.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
